From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BC-250 Liberation Project <bc250@invalid>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: gfx1013 instruction-fetch fault probe

Diagnostic. Report-only -- it changes no control flow and fixes nothing.

The open BC-250 compute defect is that the second heavy GPU phase of a
multi-phase workload dies on a GPUVM fault. The fault is always an SQC (inst)
read, i.e. the shader-instruction cache, so the wave's PC was already wrong
before the fault was raised.

Nine faults collected across separate boots with ASLR active (GabriWar,
docs/08-address-corruption.md) show seven sharing an identical shape:

  0xffb5506bb000  0xffe8464bb000  0xff14126bb000  0xff550dabb000
  0xff26f76bb000  0xfffd1e6bb000  0xff64aa2bb000

Top byte 0xff, low 20 bits 0xbb000, only bits [39:20] varying with ASLR. The
process's own code objects live at 0x7f..., and 0x7f -> 0xff is a single bit:
bit 47, the canonical-form boundary. The low bits are a plausible entry point.
So this is one wrong bit in the top byte, not a garbage address -- and the top
byte is exactly COMPUTE_PGM_HI, which carries address bits [47:40] and is
8 bits wide.

This probe records, for gfx1013 only, the raw interrupt vector and the
bit-47-cleared reconstruction, so the candidate can be checked against the
faulting process's GPU VA map offline. If the candidate consistently resolves
to a mapped code object, the defect is isolated to the top byte of the shader
program address and the remaining question is who sets bit 47.

It deliberately does not read COMPUTE_PGM_LO/HI. Those are per-pipe CP
registers behind GRBM indexing and srbm_mutex; this handler runs in hard-IRQ
context, so reading them here would deadlock. (Reading them from userspace via
debugfs amdgpu_regs is also known to hang this board.) That measurement needs a
process-context path and is not attempted here.

Gated by amdgpu.bc250_fault_probe (default on, 0 disables). The module
parameter doubles as the runtime tell for `arieltune apu patches`.

Signed-off-by: BC-250 Liberation Project <bc250@invalid>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
  *
  */
 #include <linux/firmware.h>
+#include <linux/moduleparam.h>
 #include <linux/pci.h>
 
 #include <drm/drm_cache.h>
@@ -96,6 +97,26 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * BC-250 / gfx1013 instruction-fetch fault probe.
+ *
+ * Faults on this part arrive as SQC (inst) reads from an address whose top
+ * byte is 0xff where the process's own code objects live at 0x7f..., i.e. a
+ * 48-bit address with bit 47 set that should be clear. Everything below bit 47
+ * looks like a valid entry point. This probe records the raw interrupt vector
+ * plus the bit-47-cleared reconstruction so the candidate can be checked
+ * against the faulting process's GPU VA map offline.
+ *
+ * Report-only: no register reads, no locks, no control-flow change. It runs
+ * inside the existing ratelimited fault print, which is hard-IRQ context --
+ * reading the CP's COMPUTE_PGM_LO/HI here would need srbm_mutex and would
+ * deadlock, so that measurement needs a process-context path instead.
+ */
+static int bc250_fault_probe = 1;
+module_param_named(bc250_fault_probe, bc250_fault_probe, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(bc250_fault_probe,
+	"BC-250: extended gfx1013 GPUVM fault diagnostics (0 = off, 1 = on)");
+
 static int gmc_v10_0_process_interrupt(struct amdgpu_device *adev,
 				       struct amdgpu_irq_src *source,
 				       struct amdgpu_iv_entry *entry)
@@ -180,6 +201,23 @@
 	if (status != 0)
 		hub->vmhub_funcs->print_l2_protection_fault_status(adev,
 								   status);
+
+	if (bc250_fault_probe &&
+	    amdgpu_ip_version(adev, GC_HWIP, 0) == IP_VERSION(10, 1, 3)) {
+		dev_err(adev->dev,
+			"  BC-250 probe: src_data[0]=0x%08x src_data[1]=0x%08x retry=%d exe=%d write=%d\n",
+			entry->src_data[0], entry->src_data[1],
+			!!(entry->src_data[1] &
+			   AMDGPU_GMC9_FAULT_SOURCE_DATA_RETRY),
+			!!(entry->src_data[1] &
+			   AMDGPU_GMC9_FAULT_SOURCE_DATA_EXE),
+			!!(entry->src_data[1] &
+			   AMDGPU_GMC9_FAULT_SOURCE_DATA_WRITE));
+		dev_err(adev->dev,
+			"  BC-250 probe: fault 0x%016llx bit47=%d candidate 0x%016llx\n",
+			addr, (int)((addr >> 47) & 1),
+			addr & ~(1ULL << 47));
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
